Fixes: de9647efeaa9 ("platform/x86: intel-vbtn: Only activate tablet mode switch on 2-in-1's")
Signed-off-by: Hans de Goede <hdegoede@redhat.com>
Signed-off-by: Andy Shevchenko <andriy.shevchenko@linux.intel.com>

Here is the root cause:
The bug arises from the use of a single sparse keymap that combines both button and switch entries, which can lead to incorrect reporting of device capabilities to userspace. This can result in userspace being informed about switches that do not exist or are not applicable, particularly in devices that do not have the necessary hardware features. The split into separate keymaps allows for more accurate representation of the device's capabilities.

